{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CfrvAnPyoaXuBcSEi1n4y","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0151FzRbSemPughbbjtWWLme","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/alustosa/git/model-routing-eval/.work/agent-eval/2026-10-09-claude-haiku-5-5-effort-low/cases/r05_fromager_version_prebuilt/docs/concepts/package-settings.rst"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6583,"cache_read_input_tokens":91250,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6583},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"11316fc5-3114-41d9-8938-693c3d7008eb","uuid":"eff364d5-8f61-41cf-98d0-16286e34815e","timestamp":"2026-10-09T15:41:49.259Z","request_id":"req_011CfrvAmhoX4am6ZsgXRBQm","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_0151FzRbSemPughbbjtWWLme":{"file_path":"/home/alustosa/git/model-routing-eval/.work/agent-eval/2026-10-09-claude-haiku-5-5-effort-low/cases/r05_fromager_version_prebuilt/docs/concepts/package-settings.rst"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0151FzRbSemPughbbjtWWLme","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tPackage Settings\n2\t================\n3\t\n4\tFromager uses a layered settings system to configure how each package\n5\tis resolved, downloaded, patched, and built.  Settings flow from YAML\n6\tfiles on disk through a merge pipeline into a single facade object\n7\tused by the build pipeline.\n8\t\n9\t.. seealso::\n10\t\n11\t   :doc:`/reference/config-reference` documents every configuration\n12\t   field.  :doc:`architecture-overview` maps the major subsystems.\n13\t\n14\tSettings Loading Flow\n15\t---------------------\n16\t\n17\t.. code-block:: text\n18\t\n19\t   CLI flags\n20\t   (--settings-file, --settings-dir, --patches-dir)\n21\t         │\n22\t         ▼\n23\t   Settings.from_files()\n24\t   ├── Load settings.yaml ──► SettingsFile (global config)\n25\t   └── Glob settings/*.yaml ──► PackageSettings (one per package)\n26\t         │\n27\t         ▼\n28\t   Settings object (held by WorkContext)\n29\t         │\n30\t         │  package_build_info(\"torch\")  (on demand, cached)\n31\t         ▼\n32\t   PackageBuildInfo\n33\t   (single facade used by the build pipeline)\n34\t\n35\t``PackageBuildInfo`` objects are created lazily the first time a\n36\tpackage is queried and cached for the rest of the run.\n37\t\n38\tDirectory Structure\n39\t-------------------\n40\t\n41\t.. code-block:: text\n42\t\n43\t   overrides/\n44\t   ├── settings.yaml              # Global settings\n45\t   ├── settings/                  # Per-package settings\n46\t   │   ├── torch.yaml\n47\t   │   ├── flash-attn.yaml\n48\t   │   └── ...\n49\t   └── patches/                   # Patches\n50\t       ├── torch/                 # Unversioned (all versions)\n51\t       │   ├── 001-fix.patch\n52\t       │   └── cpu/               # Variant-specific\n53\t       │       └── 002-cpu.patch\n54\t       └── torch-2.4.0/           # Version-specific\n55\t           └── 001-ver.patch\n56\t\n57\tPackage YAML filenames use the canonicalized package name (lowercase,\n58\thyphens).  All three directories are configurable via CLI flags.\n59\t\n60\tMerge Order\n61\t-----------\n62\t\n63\tSettings are merged from least-specific to most-specific.  Later\n64\tlayers override earlier ones:\n65\t\n66\t.. code-block:: text\n67\t\n68\t   ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n69\t   │  1. Pydantic field defaults                      │\n70\t   │     (empty env, default build options, etc.)     │\n71\t   │                                                  │\n72\t   │  2. Global settings.yaml                         │\n73\t   │     (SBOM config, global changelog)              │\n74\t   │                                                  │\n75\t   │  3. Per-package YAML file                        │\n76\t   │     (env, resolver, build options, patches, ...) │\n77\t   │                                                  │\n78\t   │  4. Variant overrides (within package YAML)      │\n79\t   │     (env vars, pre_built, wheel_server_url)      │\n80\t   │                                                  │\n81\t   │  5. Version-specific patches and changelog       │\n82\t   │     (patches/<pkg>-<version>/, changelog entries)│\n83\t   │                                                  │\n84\t   │  6. Override plugin hooks (runtime)              │\n85\t   │     (update_extra_environ can mutate env vars)   │\n86\t   └──────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n87\t\n88\tFor environment variables specifically, the merge order within a\n89\tsingle ``get_extra_environ()`` call is: parallel-jobs settings, build\n90\tenvironment paths, package-level ``env``, then variant-level ``env``.\n91\tEntries can reference earlier values using ``$VAR`` template syntax.\n92\t\n93\tPackageBuildInfo Facade\n94\t-----------------------\n95\t\n96\t``PackageBuildInfo`` is the single interface the build pipeline uses to\n97\tquery all package configuration.  It wraps a ``PackageSettings`` and\n98\tadds variant awareness, patch discovery, and template resolution.\n99\t\n100\t.. list-table::\n101\t   :header-rows: 1\n102\t   :widths: 25 75\n103\t\n104\t   * - Category\n105\t     - What it provides\n106\t   * - **Identity**\n107\t     - Package name, variant, whether a config file exists, override\n108\t       plugin module\n109\t   * - **Resolution**\n110\t     - Sdist server URL, include wheels/sdists flags, platform\n111\t       filtering, per-package cooldown override\n112\t   * - **Build config**\n113\t     - Environment variables, parallel jobs, exclusive build flag,\n114\t       PEP 517 config settings, build directory\n115\t   * - **Source**\n116\t     - Download URL and filename templates with ``${version}``\n117\t       substitution, git submodule options\n118\t   * - **Patches**\n119\t     - Merged list of unversioned + version-specific + variant-specific\n120\t       patch files, sorted by filename\n121\t   * - **Metadata**\n122\t     - Build tag (from changelog length), annotations, PURL config,\n123\t       pyproject.toml overrides\n124\t\n125\tSee :doc:`/reference/config-reference` for the full field reference.\n126\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"11316fc5-3114-41d9-8938-693c3d7008eb","uuid":"b4e952a9-4f77-4929-969a-3aa374e7bd75","timestamp":"2026-10-09T15:41:49.303Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/alustosa/git/model-routing-eval/.work/agent-eval/2026-10-09-claude-haiku-5-5-effort-low/cases/r05_fromager_version_prebuilt/docs/concepts/package-settings.rst","content":"Package Settings\n================\n\nFromager uses a layered settings system to configure how each package\nis resolved, downloaded, patched, and built.  Settings flow from YAML\nfiles on disk through a merge pipeline into a single facade object\nused by the build pipeline.\n\n.. seealso::\n\n   :doc:`/reference/config-reference` documents every configuration\n   field.  :doc:`architecture-overview` maps the major subsystems.\n\nSettings Loading Flow\n---------------------\n\n.. code-block:: text\n\n   CLI flags\n   (--settings-file, --settings-dir, --patches-dir)\n         │\n         ▼\n   Settings.from_files()\n   ├── Load settings.yaml ──► SettingsFile (global config)\n   └── Glob settings/*.yaml ──► PackageSettings (one per package)\n         │\n         ▼\n   Settings object (held by WorkContext)\n         │\n         │  package_build_info(\"torch\")  (on demand, cached)\n         ▼\n   PackageBuildInfo\n   (single facade used by the build pipeline)\n\n``PackageBuildInfo`` objects are created lazily the first time a\npackage is queried and cached for the rest of the run.\n\nDirectory Structure\n-------------------\n\n.. code-block:: text\n\n   overrides/\n   ├── settings.yaml              # Global settings\n   ├── settings/                  # Per-package settings\n   │   ├── torch.yaml\n   │   ├── flash-attn.yaml\n   │   └── ...\n   └── patches/                   # Patches\n       ├── torch/                 # Unversioned (all versions)\n       │   ├── 001-fix.patch\n       │   └── cpu/               # Variant-specific\n       │       └── 002-cpu.patch\n       └── torch-2.4.0/           # Version-specific\n           └── 001-ver.patch\n\nPackage YAML filenames use the canonicalized package name (lowercase,\nhyphens).  All three directories are configurable via CLI flags.\n\nMerge Order\n-----------\n\nSettings are merged from least-specific to most-specific.  Later\nlayers override earlier ones:\n\n.. code-block:: text\n\n   ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n   │  1. Pydantic field defaults                      │\n   │     (empty env, default build options, etc.)     │\n   │                                                  │\n   │  2. Global settings.yaml                         │\n   │     (SBOM config, global changelog)              │\n   │                                                  │\n   │  3. Per-package YAML file                        │\n   │     (env, resolver, build options, patches, ...) │\n   │                                                  │\n   │  4. Variant overrides (within package YAML)      │\n   │     (env vars, pre_built, wheel_server_url)      │\n   │                                                  │\n   │  5. Version-specific patches and changelog       │\n   │     (patches/<pkg>-<version>/, changelog entries)│\n   │                                                  │\n   │  6. Override plugin hooks (runtime)              │\n   │     (update_extra_environ can mutate env vars)   │\n   └──────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n\nFor environment variables specifically, the merge order within a\nsingle ``get_extra_environ()`` call is: parallel-jobs settings, build\nenvironment paths, package-level ``env``, then variant-level ``env``.\nEntries can reference earlier values using ``$VAR`` template syntax.\n\nPackageBuildInfo Facade\n-----------------------\n\n``PackageBuildInfo`` is the single interface the build pipeline uses to\nquery all package configuration.  It wraps a ``PackageSettings`` and\nadds variant awareness, patch discovery, and template resolution.\n\n.. list-table::\n   :header-rows: 1\n   :widths: 25 75\n\n   * - Category\n     - What it provides\n   * - **Identity**\n     - Package name, variant, whether a config file exists, override\n       plugin module\n   * - **Resolution**\n     - Sdist server URL, include wheels/sdists flags, platform\n       filtering, per-package cooldown override\n   * - **Build config**\n     - Environment variables, parallel jobs, exclusive build flag,\n       PEP 517 config settings, build directory\n   * - **Source**\n     - Download URL and filename templates with ``${version}``\n       substitution, git submodule options\n   * - **Patches**\n     - Merged list of unversioned + version-specific + variant-specific\n       patch files, sorted by filename\n   * - **Metadata**\n     - Build tag (from changelog length), annotations, PURL config,\n       pyproject.toml overrides\n\nSee :doc:`/reference/config-reference` for the full field reference.\n","numLines":126,"startLine":1,"totalLines":126}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_0151FzRbSemPughbbjtWWLme","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
