{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DkXr6VgR2TxnpwABYy4rdS","type":"tool_result","content":"258\t        req: The requirement to match.\n259\t        max_age_cutoff: If set, reject candidates published before this time.\n260\t            Age filtering is skipped for packages that have an exact\n261\t            ``==`` pin in the provider's ``constraints`` object, since\n262\t            a pin represents explicit user intent that should not be\n263\t            overridden by a heuristic.  Range constraints (``>=``,\n264\t            ``<``, etc.) still go through age filtering normally.\n265\t        age_fallback: Strategy when age filtering removes all candidates.\n266\t            ``ALL`` (default) keeps every candidate with a warning.\n267\t            ``NEWEST`` keeps only the single newest candidate.\n268\t            ``NONE`` returns an empty list, letting the caller handle it.\n269\t\n270\t    Returns list of (url, version) tuples sorted by version (highest first).\n271\t\n272\t    IMPORTANT: This bypasses resolvelib's full resolver to collect all matching\n273\t    candidates. This is safe ONLY because BaseProvider.get_dependencies() returns\n274\t    an empty list (no transitive dependencies to resolve). The empty incompatibilities\n275\t    dict means no version is ever excluded based on conflicts.\n276\t\n277\t    If get_dependencies() is ever extended to return actual dependencies, this\n278\t    function must be revisited to use resolvelib's full resolution algorithm\n279\t    (Resolver.resolve()) to properly handle dependency conflicts and backtracking.\n280\t    \"\"\"\n281\t    # Get all matching candidates directly from provider\n282\t    # instead of using resolvelib's resolver which picks just one\n283\t    identifier = provider.identify(req)\n284\t    try:\n285\t        # Bypass resolvelib's resolver to collect all matching candidates rather than\n286\t        # just the single best one. This is safe because get_dependencies() returns []\n287\t        # (no transitive deps to resolve). If get_dependencies() is ever extended,\n288\t        # this must be revisited to use resolvelib's full resolution.\n289\t        candidates = provider.find_matches(\n290\t            identifier=identifier,\n291\t            requirements={identifier: [req]},\n292\t            incompatibilities={},  # Empty - safe only because no transitive deps\n293\t        )\n294\t    except resolvelib.resolvers.ResolverException as err:\n295\t        constraint = provider.constraints.get_constraint(req.name)\n296\t        provider_desc = provider.get_provider_description()\n297\t        original_msg = str(err)\n298\t        raise resolvelib.resolvers.ResolverException(\n299\t            f\"Unable to resolve requirement specifier {req} with constraint {constraint} using {provider_desc}: {original_msg}\"\n300\t        ) from err\n301\t\n302\t    # Materialize candidates so we can iterate more than once if filtering"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"11316fc5-3114-41d9-8938-693c3d7008eb","uuid":"91a2915a-a90a-4edc-bfb6-a0e6c53926e4","timestamp":"2026-10-09T15:42:20.572Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/alustosa/git/model-routing-eval/.work/agent-eval/2026-10-09-claude-haiku-5-5-effort-low/cases/r05_fromager_version_prebuilt/src/fromager/resolver.py","content":"        req: The requirement to match.\n        max_age_cutoff: If set, reject candidates published before this time.\n            Age filtering is skipped for packages that have an exact\n            ``==`` pin in the provider's ``constraints`` object, since\n            a pin represents explicit user intent that should not be\n            overridden by a heuristic.  Range constraints (``>=``,\n            ``<``, etc.) still go through age filtering normally.\n        age_fallback: Strategy when age filtering removes all candidates.\n            ``ALL`` (default) keeps every candidate with a warning.\n            ``NEWEST`` keeps only the single newest candidate.\n            ``NONE`` returns an empty list, letting the caller handle it.\n\n    Returns list of (url, version) tuples sorted by version (highest first).\n\n    IMPORTANT: This bypasses resolvelib's full resolver to collect all matching\n    candidates. This is safe ONLY because BaseProvider.get_dependencies() returns\n    an empty list (no transitive dependencies to resolve). The empty incompatibilities\n    dict means no version is ever excluded based on conflicts.\n\n    If get_dependencies() is ever extended to return actual dependencies, this\n    function must be revisited to use resolvelib's full resolution algorithm\n    (Resolver.resolve()) to properly handle dependency conflicts and backtracking.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Get all matching candidates directly from provider\n    # instead of using resolvelib's resolver which picks just one\n    identifier = provider.identify(req)\n    try:\n        # Bypass resolvelib's resolver to collect all matching candidates rather than\n        # just the single best one. This is safe because get_dependencies() returns []\n        # (no transitive deps to resolve). If get_dependencies() is ever extended,\n        # this must be revisited to use resolvelib's full resolution.\n        candidates = provider.find_matches(\n            identifier=identifier,\n            requirements={identifier: [req]},\n            incompatibilities={},  # Empty - safe only because no transitive deps\n        )\n    except resolvelib.resolvers.ResolverException as err:\n        constraint = provider.constraints.get_constraint(req.name)\n        provider_desc = provider.get_provider_description()\n        original_msg = str(err)\n        raise resolvelib.resolvers.ResolverException(\n            f\"Unable to resolve requirement specifier {req} with constraint {constraint} using {provider_desc}: {original_msg}\"\n        ) from err\n\n    # Materialize candidates so we can iterate more than once if filtering","numLines":45,"startLine":258,"totalLines":1399}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01DkXr6VgR2TxnpwABYy4rdS","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
