{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CfrvQgdMHXJv2z36qWTpb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The version-specific pre-built and wheel server URL override now works end to end, and the START phase re-resolves the download URL when the resolved version's setting differs from the variant default. Both target test files pass (227 tests), and so do the neighbouring bootstrapper, override, and wheel test files (251 tests). I didn't commit anything.\n\nTwo of the spec items were already in the code, so I only added tests for them:\n- **`_models.py`:** a bare `versions:` already coerces to `{}`, and an omitted key already defaults to `{}`.\n- **`wheels.get_wheel_server_urls`:** already takes `version` and uses the version-specific URL.\n\nWhat changed:\n- **`_pbi.py`:** `is_pre_built()` and `get_wheel_server_url()` strip the local segment for the YAML lookup. The `is_pre_built` hook goes through `overrides.find_and_invoke` with `_default_is_pre_built` only when a version is given. The `pre_built` and `wheel_server_url` properties delegate to these methods. The `versionadded` directives are now 0.95.0.\n- **`_start.py`:** `_re_resolve_url` is added. `run()` computes the pre-built flag first, then re-resolves before the graph update and the seen-check. On `None` it logs a warning and keeps the original URL.\n- **Docs:** a \"Version-Specific Overrides\" section in `package-settings.rst`, and a note on the hook in `hooks-and-overrides.rst`.\n- **Tests:** new cases in both test files. The existing `test_sets_pbi_pre_built_before_prepare_source` used a bare `Mock` that would now trigger a re-resolve, so I changed its mock to match.\n\nChoices I made where the spec left room:\n- The `is_pre_built` hook receives the original version with its local segment. Only the YAML lookup strips it.\n- If the variant isn't configured at all, `is_pre_built` still returns `False` before the hook runs, as before.\n- In the source path, a `ResolverException` from `find_all_matching_from_provider` is treated as `None`, the same as an empty result.\n\nLint and types:\n- `hatch run lint:fix` reformatted an unrelated import in `bootstrap_requirement_resolver.py`. I reverted that file.\n- mypy flagged one error in my code, a `Returning Any` from the `@metrics.timeit`-wrapped `resolve_prebuilt_wheel`. I fixed it with `str(url)`.\n- Two mypy errors remain in `resolver.py` (lines 1219 and 1342). I didn't touch that file, so they predate this change."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4796,"cache_read_input_tokens":195781,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4796},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"11316fc5-3114-41d9-8938-693c3d7008eb","uuid":"f83848e6-7c6c-4fd5-acf5-fdd9ed82ab9b","timestamp":"2026-10-09T15:45:00.215Z","request_id":"req_011CfrvQgKjxcvR4vz2jVRSm"}
